# Tracer: ReOfRealPlusImagScaled checks both rectangular coefficients in R.
# Before (incorrectly accepted):
# re(i + i) = i
# re(0 + i * i) = 0
# Former behavior: either complex coefficient could invalidate the formula.
# Now: both real-coefficient premises are checked and retained.
forall a, b R:
    re(a + b * i) = a
    a = re(b * i + a)
re(i + i) = 0
# Boundary: checking only the first coefficient does not justify the second old line.
# Executable negatives: hcx_arithmetic_guards::false_operand_orders_and_complex_second_coefficients_reject.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -strict -lang en -f examples/proof_nodes/equal/by_builtin_rule/re_of_real_plus_imag_scaled_real_guards.lit
